<h1>Privacy</h1>

<p>Junior Golf Wales is a directory of publicly available junior golf event
listings. Browsing the site does not require an account and we do not track
individual visitors beyond standard, anonymous web server logs.</p>

<h2>Event submissions</h2>
<p>If you submit an event using our <a href="/submit-event">submission
form</a>, we collect the event details you provide and the email address you
give us, solely so we can review and, if appropriate, publish the event.
Submitted contact details are not published or shared, and are used only for
this purpose.</p>

<h2>Event registration forms</h2>
<p>Some events have an optional signup form built by the hosting club. If you
fill one in, the information you provide is used only to register you for
that event and is shared with the organising club. It is automatically
deleted 30 days after the event date. We do not use this information for
marketing or share it with anyone beyond the organising club.</p>

<h2>Club accounts</h2>
<p>Clubs can create an account to manage their own event listings. We store
the name, email address, and a securely hashed password for each club
account. This is used only to operate the club login and is not shared or
published.</p>

<h2>Cookies</h2>
<p>This site does not use tracking or advertising cookies. Club and admin
logins use a session cookie that identifies you as logged in — nothing else.</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>Questions about this policy or your data can be sent via the
<a href="/contact">contact page</a>.</p>

